{"name":"Balsam Branch","hex":"#36574e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"balsam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet-smelling oil or resin derived from various plants.","A plant or tree yielding such substance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat or anoint with balsam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balsam"},{"term":"branch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The woody part of a tree arising from the trunk and usually dividing.","Any of the parts of something that divides like the branch of a tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arise from the trunk or a larger branch of a tree.","To produce branches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/branch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balsam","blocks":[{"text":"Balsam is the resinous exudate which forms on certain kinds of trees and shrubs, particularly species belonging to genera such as Myroxylon, Abies, Copaifera, Styrax, and Populus. They may occur naturally as resinous exudates following injury to bark or wood tissues. Balsam owes its name to the biblical Balm of Gilead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG/330px-Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balsam"},{"title":"Branch","blocks":[{"text":"A branch, also called a ramus in botany, is a stem that grows off from another stem, or when structures like veins in leaves are divided into smaller veins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Branches_%28DSC_0326%29.jpg/330px-Branches_%28DSC_0326%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branch"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg/500px-Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th